The tick fires the due timer lines but leaves the nearest deadline where it was.
Once that line fired the timer would wake for a deadline already past, every tick;
the nearest deadline lies ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: the timer wakes for a deadline already past

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -448,7 +448,6 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
             nearest = irq->deadline;
         }
     }
-    nearest_deadline = nearest;
     if (!tick_before(sched_ticks, nearest_release)) {
         release();
     }
